# L §8.3 LOAD-BAND (round 9): "band <b> in <version>: rows unordered, overlapping or with a gap at <x>", "x is the
# lower end of the first row, in the table's order, that doesn't start where the row before it ends: an overlap, a
# gap or a row out of order"; L §5.9: rows "meet without a gap, closed against open; int arguments are checked over
# the integers".
# rows written out of order, [5, 18) then [0, 5): the second row doesn't start at 18, where the first ends: x = 0,
# its lower end.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2016-03-01
  start 2015-11-01
  end 2016-10-31

source s "s"
band b(n: num): int

version v
  cite s
  governs 2015-11..
  known 2015-09-07
  b: [5, 18) = 1
  b: [0, 5) = 2
=== expect
refused: LOAD-BAND band b in v: rows unordered, overlapping or with a gap at 0 (m.tally:15)
